1: //! Live events: a streaming view over the YAML input.
2: //!
3: //! This module implements `LiveEvents`, an Events source that pulls items directly
4: //! from the underlying `granit_parser::Parser` as it scans the input string.
5: //! Unlike `ReplayEvents`, which iterates over a pre-recorded buffer, live events
6: //! are produced on demand and reflect the current position of the parser.
7: //!
8: //! Responsibilities and behavior:
9: //! - Skip parser-level stream/document boundary markers so consumers see only
10: //!   logical YAML nodes: container starts/ends, scalars, and aliases.
11: //! - Track and record anchors for both scalars and containers. When an alias is
12: //!   encountered later, the previously recorded sequence of events for that
13: //!   anchor is injected (replayed) back into the stream.
14: //! - Enforce alias-bomb hardening via `AliasLimits` and account replayed events
15: //!   per anchor and in total. `BudgetEnforcer` can also be attached to limit raw
16: //!   event production and retained anchor copies.
17: //! - Maintain a single-item lookahead buffer to implement `peek()`, and keep
18: //!   `last_location` to improve error reporting.
19: //!
20: //! `LiveEvents` is single-pass and does not support rewinding. Aliases expand by
21: //! injecting previously recorded buffers; normal parsing continues after the
22: //! injection is exhausted.
