1: # Focused city installation
2: 
3: Street-scale map views refine the regional terrain with one complete canonical
4: settlement. The renderer requests the closest observer-admitted settlement
5: within two kilometres when the vertical view span is at most two kilometres.
6: Case-site markers never request scenes or reveal actual case locations.
7: 
8: The browser fetches the read-only city endpoint and carries its response as
9: opaque text. The existing worker pool prepares supported terrain, ground
10: samples, paving and every exterior building program. It requests no occupied
11: interiors, furniture, scatter or tactical actors. Native installation admits the
12: source, known settlement focus, full scene document and exact preparation ticket
13: before consuming the completed regional-map product.
14: 
15: Building installation queues every primary and distant placement. The existing
16: GPU city assembler publishes a marker on the exact candidate root. Failure
17: preserves the previous city buffers; an older owner's readiness flag cannot
18: acknowledge the new candidate. Successful assembly and render preparation
19: replace the previous city, independently of actor preparation or replacement.
20: Status exposes `city_requested`, `city_installation` and `city_visible`.
21: 
22: Canonical playable ground and all configured vista rings use the same producer
23: as actor scenery. The worker also retains the implicit geological patch that
24: owns any landform cutout; its displayed triangles participate in ground queries.
25: Streets and yards reuse the worker's terrain-clipped batches.
26: Their shared clipping producer includes walkable landform faces after removing
27: the ordinary terrain inside the cutout. Actor workers carry the already-generated
28: patch into paving preparation; neither view generates a second patch for roads.
29: Geographic uploads reverse triangle indices without changing actor mesh
30: handles. The city root and GPU frame carry local east/up/north metres into the
31: window's east/up/south frame, including absolute source elevation. Reanchoring
32: updates the root, one GPU frame buffer and material-coordinate uniforms without
33: regenerating terrain or buildings. Soil, stone and wear patterns stay fixed in
34: canonical city coordinates.
35: Terrain uses the same standard sky-environment lighting as paving and building

